    "body": "> > I may open a new PR specifically for setting a `relatedTarget`-like attribute on popover events that point to the element with `popovertarget`/`invoketarget`.\r\n> \r\n> Would the behavior be different from what you're proposing here? While you're right that (by design) you can't cancel `beforetoggle` for a \"closing\" transition, the information about who closed you might still be interesting?\r\n\r\nMy guess is that it would be similar to this, but not part of the \"light dismiss behavior.\r\n\r\nI can see use cases where you want to know which element triggered the popover to show, but less so to know what caused it to \"light dismiss\", especially if you can't change the outcome.",
